    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. We've had some issues though where the loads seem stable when we first set them, but then things get slightly shifted or knocked out of alignment during transit or when the floor vibrates from the forklifts. Is there anything else we should be looking out for to prevent random shifts in the stack stability?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To prevent shifting during transit or vibration, use load securement methods such as shrink-wrapping or strapping around the pallet load. Consider placing dunnage or void fill between the load and the pallet deck to minimize movement. Furthermore, ensure your forklift operators use slow, controlled movements when accessing or moving the racks. Regular inspection of pallet integrity and racking connections is also essential maintenance.",
      "source": "target",
