      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "These subtle disruptions are often caused by micro-vibrations or very minor, repeated impacts from daily warehouse activity. High-frequency vibrations from nearby machinery or even tires rolling past the rack area can gradually loosen packing or straps. Also, unevenly worn floor surfaces can introduce slight, unexpected lateral forces during passing. Addressing these involves improving floor leveling and ensuring your racking structure dampens vibrations.",
